.\" punkhazard(6) -- mdoc(7), the FreeBSD manual format.
.Dd September 25, 2026
.Dt PUNKHAZARD 6
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm punkhazard
.Nd retro console-style game launcher
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Op Cm ui
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Cm add Ar path
.Op Fl -title Ar name
.Op Fl -exec Ar path
.Op Fl -args Ar string
.Op Fl -genre Ar name
.Op Fl -developer Ar name
.Op Fl -year Ar year
.Op Fl -desc Ar text
.Op Fl -cover Ar file
.Op Fl -no-build
.Op Fl -link
.Nm
.Cm ls
.Nm
.Cm info | run | rm Ar slug
.Nm
.Cm paths | version | help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a full-screen launcher for games kept in a local library.
It presents a grid of box art with a details and options panel, and a
system monitor, and is driven by keyboard, mouse or gamepad.
It runs on X11 and on Wayland from the same binary, choosing between them
at run time.
.Pp
With no command,
.Nm
starts the graphical launcher.
Every operation it performs is also available from the shell, so a library
can be built and inspected by scripts.
.Pp
.Nm
is the parent process of the game it launches: it waits for the game to
exit, then records the elapsed time.
It makes no network connections.
.Ss Commands
.Bl -tag -width "add path"
.It Cm ui
Run the graphical launcher.
This is the default.
.It Cm add Ar path
Import a game.
.Ar path
may be an executable, a directory, a source tree, or an archive
.Pq tar, gz, bz2, xz, zst, zip .
An archive is extracted first; a source tree is built with the first
matching recipe from
.Pa install.lua ;
the resulting tree is then scanned for an entry point.
The chosen slug is printed on standard output.
.It Cm ls
List the library on standard output, one game per line, as tab-separated
fields: slug, title, genre, year, playtime, launch count, favourite.
.It Cm info Ar slug
Print one game's record as tab-separated key/value lines.
.It Cm run Ar slug
Launch a game without starting the graphical launcher.
The game's own exit status is passed through.
.It Cm rm Ar slug
Remove a game and everything under its directory.
.It Cm paths
Print the directories in use.
.It Cm version
Print the version.
.It Cm help
Print a usage summary.
.El
.Ss Options
.Bl -tag -width "-developer name"
.It Fl v
Verbose: report each step on standard error.
Must precede the command.
.It Fl -title Ar name
Display name.
Defaults to the file or directory name.
The slug is derived from it.
.It Fl -exec Ar path
Entry point, relative to the imported tree.
Overrides the automatic scan.
.It Fl -args Ar string
Arguments passed to the game.
Quoting is understood; no shell is involved.
.It Fl -genre Ar name , Fl -developer Ar name , Fl -year Ar year
Metadata, shown in the launcher and searched by the filter.
.It Fl -desc Ar text
One-line description.
.It Fl -cover Ar file
Box art
.Pq png or jpeg ,
copied into the game's directory.
.It Fl -no-build
Import a source tree without running a build recipe.
.It Fl -link
Register the game where it is instead of copying it.
.Va exec
and
.Va workdir
are then absolute, and nothing is duplicated.
.El
.Ss Keys
.Bl -tag -width "PageUp, PageDown" -compact
.It Ic arrows , h j k l
Move around the grid.
.It Ic Tab
Move focus between the grid and the options panel.
.It Ic PageUp , PageDown
Move a screenful.
.It Ic Home , End
First or last entry.
.It Ic Return , Space
Launch, or activate the highlighted option.
.It Ic /
Filter the library.
.It Ic B , *
Toggle favourite.
Favourites sort first.
.It Ic S
Cycle the sort key.
.It Ic R
Rescan the library from disk.
.It Ic T
Cycle theme.
.It Ic C
Toggle the CRT post-process.
.It Ic F11 , F
Toggle fullscreen.
.It Ic F1 , ?
Key help.
.It Ic Esc
Close an overlay, or clear the filter.
.It Ic Q
Quit.
.El
.Pp
On a gamepad, the d-pad or left stick moves,
.Ic A
launches,
.Ic B
backs out,
.Ic X
focuses the options panel,
.Ic Y
favourites, the shoulder buttons page, and
.Ic Back
cycles the sort key.
All bindings are defined in
.Pa keys.lua
and may be changed without recompiling.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width PUNKHAZARD_ROOT
.It Ev PUNKHAZARD_ROOT
The library directory.
If unset,
.Ev XDG_DATA_HOME Ns Pa /punkhazard
is used, and failing that
.Pa ~/.local/share/punkhazard .
.It Ev PUNKHAZARD_LUA
Directory holding the Lua policy files.
Defaults to the installed
.Pa share/punkhazard/lua .
Set it to run from a build tree.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "<root>/games/<slug>/manifest" -compact
.It Pa <root>/config.lua
User settings, merged over the shipped defaults.
.It Pa <root>/games/<slug>/manifest
One game's record: text,
.Ql key = value ,
one per line.
.It Pa <root>/games/<slug>/root/
The game's own files.
.It Pa <root>/games/<slug>/cover.png
Box art.
.It Pa <root>/games/<slug>/install.log
Transcript of the import and build.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/punkhazard
Default library root.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
.Cm run
instead exits with the status of the game it launched.
A usage error exits 2.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Import a prebuilt binary with metadata:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
punkhazard add ~/games/quake/quake --title Quake \e
    --genre FPS --year 1996 --developer "id Software"
.Ed
.Pp
Import and build a source tree:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
punkhazard add ~/src/openttd --title OpenTTD
.Ed
.Pp
Register something already installed, without copying it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
punkhazard add /usr/local/bin/nethack --link --title NetHack
.Ed
.Pp
The five games with the most launches:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
punkhazard ls | sort -t"$(printf '\et')" -k6 -rn | head -5 | cut -f2
.Ed
.Pp
Everything never actually played:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
punkhazard ls | awk -F'\et' '$5 == "never" { print $2 }'
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr make 1 ,
.Xr tar 1 ,
.Xr hier 7 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh STANDARDS
The library root follows the XDG Base Directory Specification when
.Ev XDG_DATA_HOME
is set.
The default install prefix follows
.Xr hier 7 .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An orpheus497
.Sh CAVEATS
The entry-point scanner is a heuristic.
When it chooses the wrong file, pass
.Fl -exec .
.Pp
Cover art is decoded by a vendored copy of
.Nm stb_image ,
which is not a hardened decoder.
It parses whatever image files are present in the library directory.
